jigsaw is the unforgettable villain in  the source series but he's not just a  creepy puppet  he's a deeply disturbed man whose morals  are as warped as they are eerily  understandable  this is the story of john kramer billy  the puppet  and where it all began there's no doubt  that jigsaw's life took a deeply dark  turn  yet before he became jigsaw john kramer  led a genuinely upright life  as civil engineer kramer was utterly  dedicated to making cities better places  to live with his business partner a  lawyer named art blank  he started a foundation with the goal of  creating affordable housing for working  families  the foundation's first major project was  a meat packing plant  this was presumably undertaken to  provide jobs for blue-collar workers in  new york city  but this planted a far darker destiny it  would become a base of operations for  jon  after he became a serial murderer  unsurprisingly  jigsaw took full advantage of the plan's  capacity for grotesque horror  we often imagined serial killers as  extreme loners however  john kramer is very much the opposite he  was a man of and for the people  and he lived a relatively  straightforward life until it all went  wrong  prior to becoming jigsaw he married jill  turk his charitable nature rubbed off on  his wife  who kramer convinced to open up the  homewood-bound clinic aimed at helping  drug addicts recover and build new lives  jill worked at the clinic all through  her pregnancy with their first child  who kramer hoped to name gideon  alongside her team of nurses  jill helped people hoping to kick their  opiate addictions and she did so with  kindness  strength and perseverance though he  encouraged her to start the clinic  kramer's increasing sense of the danger  of jill's job began to weigh on him  particularly as her pregnancy progressed  much of kramer's pre-jigsaw life would  extend into his career as a serial  killer  the knowledge he'd gained as an engineer  and builder would eventually come to  fruition in his infamous and deadly  contraptions  in time john kramer met a man named  willian easton at a party thrown at the  clinic  easton was the head of umbrella  insurance and he revealed an algorithm  his company used to distribute care  essentially placing a concrete value on  each individual human life  everybody thinks we're the bad guys  nobody mentions the millions of people  we help every year  without incident kramer was horrified  both by the concept and the variables  eastern used he thought that the  equation was faulty because it didn't  take into account a patient's will to  live  this was a brutal lesson in the  mathematics of morality one that would  leave kramer forever changed  kramer became more and more uneasy about  jill's workplace and with good reason  one night at the clinic as he waited to  pick up his wife kramer got between two  patients about to come to blows one of  the men  cecil adams pulled a knife on john  kramer was able to successfully talk  adams down  convincing him to drop the knife and  even managing to deliver a lecture  on how one's mistakes can spiral out of  control and affect society at large  despite kramer's warning cecil adams  returned to the clinic  where he threatened jill with a knife  and forced her to open the door  he backed the visibly pregnant gillip  against the wall and commanded her to  stay put while he stole supplies of  methadone  leaving with the stolen medication cecil  accidentally hit jill in the stomach  jill began to bleed and collapse to the  floor realizing that he may have hurt  jill's unborn child  cecil ran from the clinic kramer was  waiting out front to pick up his wife  when he saw cecil leaving in a panic he  ran in to see if anyone was hurt  jon found his wife bleeding out on the  floor and took her to a nearby hospital  jill and john's first child gideon had  been lost they were utterly devastated  and would never attempt to have another  child  gideon's death took john to a dark place  he began refusing to see his wife or go  to work  he abandoned his mission to build  housing for the needy his withdrawal  from the world was so complete that  neither jill nor kramer's business  partner art blank  knew where to find him they finally  found john in his workshop where he had  been building billy the puppet  blank urged kramer not to walk away from  the needy families they had helped  kramer was blank argued their savior  and they needed him now more than ever  sadly kramer was unmoved  jill delivered a parting blow telling  jon that she suffered as much if not  more from gideon's death she separated  from jon soon after  after splitting from jill jon began to  deteriorate  cramer was diagnosed with colon cancer  and an additional tumor in the frontal  lobe of his brain and started  chemotherapy  however he was late in beginning his  treatment as one of the hospital's  residents accidentally mixed up his  imaging results with another patient  his name is john dr gordon  he's a very interesting person  by the time the tumor in kramer's brain  was discovered the doctors believed it  to be inoperable  as a result kramer desperately began to  seek out experimental cancer treatments  the clock was ticking and the odds were  against him  kramer needed approval from his medical  insurance companies undergo a radical  cancer treatment in norway he attended a  meeting with william easton the  insurance executive would previously  shaken cramer with his brutal  monetization of human life  easton claimed he couldn't cover  kramer's healthcare costs based on the  aforementioned algorithms umbrella  insurance used in all cases  as eastern explained in their earlier  meeting the company determined whether  or not a patient's health was a good  investment before making a decision  kramer was not considered to be a good  investment  fully convinced that he was going to die  john kramer made the decision to end his  own life  he drove off of a cliff but to his shock  he lived to tell the tale  john emerged from the crash feeling  invigorated despite his injuries  the true brush with death had made him  realize how precious life really was  kramer began to think that other people  could do with a near-death experience of  their own  he believed that if he could make people  come to faith with their own deaths  they might learn to appreciate their  lives as a result he began devising his  special games and contraptions  and started operating under his alter  ego jigsaw alongside his tricycle riding  sidekick  billy the puppet a horror icon was born  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

